  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday morning through next Sunday)\nIssued at 206 PM EDT Mon Aug 3 2026\n\nOur area is sandwiched between two high pressure systems with a \ncutoff mid-level low spinning over the region. This setup will \nsupport a general southwesterly flow and decent moisture profile \nwith PWATS ranging from 1.5-2\" each day. Expect mostly diurnal \ndriven scattered to numerous thunderstorms favoring the north and \neast CWA each day through Friday. While no widespread severe \nweather is expected, a few strong storms will be possible during \nthe period, with strong winds as the primary threat, in addition \nto localized flash flooding from the high moisture content. Model \nguidance remains in good agreement on this typical summertime \npattern persisting into next weekend. High temperatures will be \nsuppressed slightly due to the increased afternoon cloud cover \nthrough the week ranging from the 80s to low 90s and increasing to\nthe low to mid 90s into the upcoming weekend.",
